Current Version can be found [[Annoying Dog|here]]. For the Previous Versions of the Dog Residue, click [[Dog Residue/Previous_Versions|here]].

[[File:Annoying Dog (Alpha 2.7).png|thumb|261x261px|Post Alpha 2.7]]
Annoying Dog went through a few changes early on, all of which were buffs, but then stayed the same for a very long time. Starting as a 2/2 for 3G, '''Alpha 2.7''' gave it -1 cost, while '''Alpha 3.2''' gave it +1 ATK, leaving it at 3/2 for 2G.

[[File:Screenshot 107.png|thumb|259x259px|Post Alpha 3.2]]
'''Beta 28.0''' swapped its ATK and HP, giving it -1/+1, while '''Beta 56.0''' gave it +1 ATK, +2 cost and reworked it entirely, alongside Dog Residue. Before, it added a Dog Residue to the enemy's hand when played. This was done to clog their hand and force them to overdraw, as well as give them a nearly useless card. Now, it has Haste and adds a Dog Residue (which is now reasonably powerful) to your hand upon death.
[[File:Annoying Dog (Beta 28.0).png|thumb|Beta 28.0]]

